  "id": "ss.enemy.trapjaw",
  "name": "Trapjaw",
  "description": "The burrow's charger: it latches its mandibles open against their own tension and lets go, and the jaws are what throws the body. Drawn from above along +x, because the game turns this one to its heading and commits the line at the brace rather than at the launch — a body that has already chosen its lane has to be pointing down it. The open V of the jaws is the whole silhouette and the reason it cannot be confused with the Lance, which is one solid ember dart with nothing held apart. Rust body kept light enough to hold a silhouette against #372d3f earth, bone jaws, and the only ember on it is the two tips and the trigger hairs between them: the bright part is the part that is cocked. No `elite` variant on purpose — the marking only lands on wave-table bodies, and this one arrives in squads. Gameplay radius 10.",
  "tags": ["ss-enemy", "trapjaw"],
  "size": [36, 24],
